Cell["The branchial relation", "Section",
 CellID->1612953718,ExpressionUUID->"73e8aeff-5b91-f8f4-2197-47b95e25cade"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two events are branchially related when they have the same input state and \
consumed a common edge, so no single history contains both. ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<BranchialEdges\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "33e490f1-5bc8-e939-619b-09bb5e62b803"],
 " lists the pairs. At two steps there are three, one for each expanded \
state, since the two orders of matching the same two edges are two \
applications that share both edges:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->790826209,ExpressionUUID->"794a4309-908b-2549-2f4a-5b53213f8f93"],

